-- title:
--   Automorphisms fixing the floor and the cusp prime are trivial
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing an element $\zeta$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity, together with a ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((\mathsf q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image, under the map induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to L$, of the level-$H$ function field inside $\mathbb{Q}((\mathsf q))$, where $H=$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) is the kernel of the reduction map of unit groups attached to the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\operatorname{Frac} A = L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157)$=\mathsf q^{-1}\cdot$`jNumQ`. Let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ such that: (i) $\sigma$ fixes every element of $K$ whose Laurent series lies in the subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull (q ^ 2 * M')`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305) (itself generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by `divisorExpansions (q ^ 2 * M')`); and (ii) for every $b$ in [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L144), the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, the constant Laurent coefficient of $\sigma b$ lies in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$ if and only if that of $b$ does. Then $\sigma$ is the identity.
--
--   This is the freeness of the diamond action at the reduction of the cusp $\infty$: an $L$-automorphism of the level-$H$ function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ which acts trivially on the smaller function field and stabilises the prime of the pole chart cut out by the maximal ideal of $A$ and the constant $\mathsf q$-coefficient must be trivial. It feeds the analysis of minimal primes over the ideal generated by $j^{-1}$ in the pole chart of the two-chart integral model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_eq_refl_of_forall_apply_eq_of_forall_coeff_zero_mem_iff_chartAlgInf_xH.lean

